    }
  }, {
    "id" : "8243e8d4",
    "type" : "bulletListItem",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "(A3) required name",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " is the static "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "nullable: false",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " flag on "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "name",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " — the framework's "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "RequiredFieldRules",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " turns it into a blocking error ahead of any validator; nothing custom is needed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "cf3473bf",
    "type" : "bulletListItem",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "(A1) unique-when-present LEI",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " is the static "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "unique: true",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " flag — a single-column "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "UNIQUE",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " constraint, which most stores honour as \"unique among non-null values\", so multiple LEI-less records coexist. The flag is the backstop; the message A1 demands is the validator's job (below)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "3309d7ab",
    "type" : "bulletListItem",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "status",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " is the lifecycle enum "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "LegalEntityStatus",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " with constants "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "DRAFT",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " / "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "ACTIVE",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " / "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "RETIRED",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " (labels Draft / Active / Retired), an "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "IDisplayableEnum",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " with its "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "jsontypes.json",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " entry per the entity-class pattern. The column default "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "DRAFT",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " carries the spec's default(draft); the "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "by_status",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " index is what makes a consumer's \"exclude retired\" filter index-covered. The spec declares no transition rules between statuses — any status change is permitted, and a retired record keeps its history (rows are never deleted to retire)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "4016d210",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 3
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "The validator: "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "LegalEntityValidator",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "8a23eed1",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Two rules the descriptor flags cannot express, both carried by one "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "LegalEntityValidator",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " code-behind class beside the entity (the "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "bean-validators",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " naming convention, no registration):"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "b91da6c2",
    "type" : "numberedListItem",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "(A1) name the conflicting record.",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "unique: true",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " rejects a duplicate but its message is generic. The validator's "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "validate()",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " — when "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "lei",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " is present — resolves any other row carrying the same LEI through "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "ctx.persister()",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " and returns a "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "field-scoped blocking error on ",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "lei",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true,
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " whose message names that record (its name and LEI). At ~40 rows the per-change lookup is trivial; the DB constraint remains the race backstop."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "7e746bac",
    "type" : "numberedListItem",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "(A1-adjacent, spec rule) LEI format.",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " 20 alphanumeric characters, checked field-scoped on "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "lei",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " when present — "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "validationDescriptor",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " has no format flag, so this is the validator's second check. The column's "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "length: 20",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " bounds storage; the validator bounds content."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "7667bf61",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "No "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "configure()",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " bindings are needed — no picker scoping, no enablement gates, no cross-field reactions on a three-field form."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "48b8012c",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 3
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Persistence, migration and surface"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "06cccc1f",
    "type" : "bulletListItem",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Migration",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : ": the initial V0→V1 creation of "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "legal_entity",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " (three columns plus the framework's system columns, the "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "by_status",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " index, the "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "lei",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " unique constraint). New entity, register starts empty — no data migration, per the spec."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "90c203ab",
    "type" : "bulletListItem",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Observer sheet",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : ": a "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "@ServesEntity(entity = LegalEntity.class, mode = AccessMode.READ_WRITE)",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " sheet extending the writable entity-instance base — the register is caller-editable by design (any signed-in user, the platform's default authorization). "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "The ",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "cdm",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true,
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " domain has no sheet plane yet in this deployment",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " (the source tree is empty), so the sheet's task carries the once-per-domain scaffolding the observer-entity-sheet pattern requires: the domain caller sheet over the domain's "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "@Dao",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " factory, the seeder, and the thin writable adapter. No secret-API seam — no credential-bearing field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "efc82c1a",
    "type" : "bulletListItem",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Screens",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : ": the platform's standard screens. The edit form is the spec's default form shipped verbatim from "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "ui/cdm.party.LegalEntity.js",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " (one \"Identification\" section: name, LEI, status — no custom surface to design). The search listing is the standard candidates-driven grid over the sheet's "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "candidates",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "/"
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "candidatesCount",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " cells, filterable by "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "status",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " and searchable by "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "name",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " and "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "lei",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " — the descriptor's scalar fields make all three filterable without custom work."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "2e53b74c",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 3
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "R2's boundary (A2)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "2a4fd029",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "The register's contribution to A2 is exactly what the spec's data model says it is: "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "status",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " is persisted, indexed and exposed through the sheet, so a consumer filtering on status excludes retired records by construction. The exclusion rule itself — \"not offered as a selectable counterparty for new business\" — binds the consuming surfaces (trade booking), which this spec declares out of scope; there is no surface here that offers counterparties for new business. The task covering A2 verifies the register's half: a retired record is stored with status retired and the sheet's candidate query filters on it index-covered."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "feature-tasks-h",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 2
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Tasks"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "3f94bd41",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 3
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Task 1: The LegalEntity entity — class, enum, descriptor, migration"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "d6f0b2f9",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Depends on",
      "styles" : {
        "bold" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : ": None"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "7b6ef522",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Create the "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "cdm.party.LegalEntity",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " persistable entity per the design: the "
